Check the matched path, not the bare name, for nohiddenglob.
With nohiddenglob or nohidsysglob set, the shell asks ash_accept_glob()
whether each match may be kept, but it passed the directory entry's bare
name, so lstat() looked in the current directory rather than in the
directory being searched. For a pattern such as dir/* a match was
dropped when a hidden file of the same name happened to exist in the
current directory, and kept when it was itself hidden but the current
directory had no such file.

Copy the entry's name into place first and pass the whole path, as tab
completion already does.

